From: shadeydev <233503709+shadeydev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:03:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] server: pair names this build's matching CLI instead of npx
 t3@<version>

Intent: when the running server speaks another orchestration protocol, `t3 pair` refuses and names the CLI that matches the server. Upstream names `npx t3@<version> pair`, which runs upstream's npm package; this build publishes none. Name the runtime this machine already unpacked for the server's version (`<T3 home>/runtime/versions/<version>/t3`, `t3.exe` on Windows, used only when its `.install-complete` sentinel holds that version, as install.sh and the pinned-runtime code require), else `t3 update [--base-dir <dir>] <version>` followed by `t3 pair`. The version comes from the server's HTTP answer, so it names a path only when it is an exact version; every word is quoted with upstream's hostShellWord.

Kind: fork-only. Drop it only if this build ever publishes an npm package.

Check: apps/server/src/cli/pair.test.ts: "rejects a server on another protocol before opening its database" (no runtime: the update hint, no npx) and "names the unpacked runtime of the server's version on another protocol" (entry without sentinel: the update hint; with it: the runtime path).
Fork-Patch: pair-matching-cli.patch

